gadget: test a 250-us video service interval alongside UAC2

Target logs show missed isochronous payloads with successful MJPEG encoding,
and host JPEG errors concentrate during microphone capture. Test reduced
video service frequency while keeping the microphone and 30fps modes enabled.

High-speed endpoints with more than one transaction force bInterval=1, so
both maxpacket and interval must change. 1024 bytes at bInterval=2 provides
4.048 MB/s after 12-byte UVC headers, versus the measured 720p requirement
of about 1.28 MB/s at 30fps. This is a hardware-test candidate: high-detail
and larger-resolution payloads still require throughput validation.

--- a/scripts/uvc-gadget.sh
+++ b/scripts/uvc-gadget.sh
@@ -121,9 +121,13 @@
 		cd $OLDPWD
 	fi
 
-	# This configures the USB endpoint to allow 32x 1024 byte packets per
-	# microframe. Other valid values are 1024 and 3072.
-	echo 2048 > functions/$FUNCTION/streaming_maxpacket
+	# This configures the USB endpoint for one 1024-byte transaction every
+	# 250 us at high speed. More than one transaction forces bInterval=1,
+	# so reducing the service rate requires maxpacket <= 1024 as well.
+	# The payload budget is 4.048 MB/s with 12-byte UVC headers. Keep the
+	# camera's advertised frame rate and the UAC2 microphone unchanged.
+	echo 1024 > functions/$FUNCTION/streaming_maxpacket
+	echo 2 > functions/$FUNCTION/streaming_interval
 
 	ln -s functions/$FUNCTION configs/c.1
 }
